            "content": "Is that \"-75%\" real? A discount only means something compared to the \"was\" price.\n\nWhat the official rules say:\n• Steam: no discount for 30 days after a price increase, and the base price can't change during a sale.\n• EU law: the \"before\" price must be the lowest the seller applied in the 30+ days before the sale.\n\nOur short guide: 5 questions to ask before you buy a PC game. Rules read 2026-10-06.\n\n#pcgaming #gamedeals #steam\n\nhttps://saveandplay.com/og/real-vs-fake-game-discounts.png\n\nhttps://saveandplay.com/guides/real-vs-fake-game-discounts/?utm_source=nostr-prices&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=guide-real-vs-fake-discounts",
