            "content": "Steam key or DRM-free: what do you actually get when you press \"buy\"?\n\n• Steam: the agreement says the content is \"licensed, not sold\". The license sits on your account and the account can't be transferred.\n• GOG: sells only DRM-free games. GOG says you can back up the files, install them on as many devices as you wish, and run them with or without a launcher.\n\nNeither is better in general: it depends on what you want to do with the game later. We read the stores' own pages (2026-10-07). Not legal advice.\n\n#pcgaming #gamedeals #steam #gog #drmfree\n\nhttps://saveandplay.com/og/steam-key-vs-drm-free.png\n\nhttps://saveandplay.com/guides/steam-key-vs-drm-free/?utm_source=nostr-prices&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=guide-steam-key-vs-drm-free",
